source: crates/daemon/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Trigger or query sync. Triggering runs a sync pass in the daemon and returns when that pass finishes, however long it takes; an account still backfilling may have further pages to go

Usage: mxr sync [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --account <ACCOUNT>

      --status

      --wait
          Keep waiting until the account reports idle (no further pages), then print its status in JSON mode
      --wait-timeout-secs <WAIT_TIMEOUT_SECS>
          Maximum seconds --wait spends waiting for the account to go idle; does not bound the sync pass itself. Default 60 [default: 60]
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format. Honored by `--status`; ignored by trigger mode today [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]
  -h, --help
          Print help
